{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QGenericBase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.QGenericBase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Eval","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.map","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L138-L150","doc":"**The property transports along any ring homomorphism.**\n\nThis is the working content of \"state the property, not the ring\": a definition\nmade over `IsQGeneric` is automatically available in every specialisation — the\ngeneric-`q` field `ℚ(q)`, an archimedean evaluation at the substrate `q₀`, a\nneighbouring community's base — without restating anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qPow_sub_one_eq_mul_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qPow_sub_one_eq_mul_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L113-L136","doc":"`qⁿ - 1 = (q - 1) · [n]_q` for `n ≥ 1` — the exact boundary of the `d ≥ 2`\nchoice.\n\nSince `[n]_q` is a unit, `qⁿ - 1` is a unit **iff** `q - 1` is. The class does not\ninvert `q - 1`, so `q = 1` survives in `Spec R`; anything genuinely needing\n`(qⁿ - 1)⁻¹` is asking for `Φ₁` and should say so. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isUnit_qBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.isUnit_qBracket","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**Every quantum bracket is a unit.** This is what axiom 4 needs: quantum\ndimensions are products of brackets, so they are units too.\n\nThe proof is the whole point of choosing the cyclotomic generating set — the\nbracket is *by construction* a product of the elements the class inverts, so no\ndivisibility argument is required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qBracket","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L95-L100","doc":"The `n`-th quantum bracket in cyclotomic form: `[n]_q = ∏_{d ∣ n, d ≥ 2} Φ_d(q)`.\n\nThis is the unbalanced bracket `1 + q + ⋯ + q^{n-1}`, written so that its\nfactorisation is the definition rather than a lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.isUnit_cyclotomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.isUnit_cyclotomic","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.isUnit_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.isUnit_q","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric.mk","kind":"ctor","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.IsQGeneric","kind":"class","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/QGenericBase.lean#L85-L93","doc":"**The base-ring property.** `q` is a unit, and so is every cyclotomic\npolynomial `Φ_d` evaluated at `q`, for `d ≥ 2`.\n\nStated as a property so that the definition of a quantum universe is available\nover *any* base satisfying it, not only over the initial one\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹][Φ_d(q)⁻¹ : d ≥ 2]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}